24:Tb46,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use Split PDF","description":"Splitting a PDF lets you pull out only the pages you need from a large document: a single certificate from a scanned bundle, the signed page of a contract or a range of chapters. This split PDF tool extracts a page range into a new file, entirely inside your browser, so your document is never upload","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/split-pdf","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"Split PDF"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to extract pages from a PDF","text":"Upload the PDF and the tool reads the number of pages. Enter the “From page” and “To page” values, then press the button to download a new PDF that contains just that range. For a single page, enter the same number in both boxes."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Privacy of your document","text":"The file is processed on your device with your browser. It does not leave your computer or phone, which makes the tool suitable for bank statements, medical reports and identity documents."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"When splitting helps","text":"Upload portals often ask for a specific page: the first page of a passport, a particular page of a form or the pages of a bank statement for one month. Splitting also helps you reduce a file’s size by removing pages you do not need, and share only the relevant part of a document with someone else."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Printed page numbers versus PDF page numbers","text":"The most common mistake when splitting is mixing up the number printed on the page with the page’s position in the file. A report may have a cover page and a contents page before “Page 1”, so printed page 1 can be PDF page 3. The tool uses the position in the file, which is the number your PDF viewer shows in its page counter."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Documents people commonly split","text":"Income tax returns and Form 16 often come as one long PDF, but a bank may ask only for the first page or the acknowledgement page. Insurance policies bundle the schedule, terms and endorsements, and a claim form may need just the schedule. Scanned marksheets, rent agreements and property papers are usually combined into one file, while an application needs individual pages. Long bank statements can be reduced to the months a lender asks for."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"A simple workflow with the other PDF tools","text":"Most tasks need more than one step. To build a custom pack, first split the pages you want from each source file, then join them with the merge tool in the order required, and finally compress the result if the portal has a size limit. If you only have photos, convert them with the images to PDF tool and then split or merge the output."}]}22:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$24"}}]
